WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.275
For most of the migration,
both systems are production.

2
00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:07.373
Devices carry certificates from
both, servers trust both chains,

3
00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.863
and two sets of revocation
lists have to stay reachable.

4
00:00:10.863 --> 00:00:12.526
Five rules keep that safe.

5
00:00:12.526 --> 00:00:15.163
Each use case gets one issuer at a time.

6
00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:17.524
Trust goes up before issuance moves.

7
00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:20.975
Revocation is reachable
wherever validation happens.

8
00:00:20.975 --> 00:00:23.537
Nothing is revoked early to force a move.

9
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:25.826
And every move has a tested way back.

10
00:00:25.826 --> 00:00:28.481
The book's warning is worth remembering:

11
00:00:28.481 --> 00:00:31.862
most coexistence outages
are revocation outages.

12
00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:36.088
A list Entra ID can't reach within
ten seconds fails the sign-in.

13
00:00:36.088 --> 00:00:39.770
After the migration, the work
becomes keeping it all renewed.
